[[File:0270.JUNIO2014 BRASIL2014 Costa-Rica-vs-Inglaterra.jpg|thumb|right|Costa Rica celebrating after topping the group]]
'''Group D of the [[2014 FIFA World Cup]]''' consisted of [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]], [[Costa Rica national football team|Costa Rica]], [[England national football team|England]] and [[Italy national football team|Italy]]. It was the only group to contain more than one previous winner of the World Cup, as well as the only group in the history of the FIFA World Cup to contain three former world champions.<ref>{{cite news |last1=McIntyre |first1=Doug |title=McIntyre: Los Ticos ready to shock again |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/37398151/los-ticos-ready-another-surprise |access-date=15 December 2024 |work=ESPN.com |date=4 July 2014 |language=en}}</ref> It was also the only group with three [[2014 FIFA World Cup seeding|top 10]] [[FIFA World Ranking]] teams as of October 2013 (ranking date for final draw) and at the start of the competition. These unique characteristics made this group to be widely considered as one of the tournament's three [[Group of death|groups of death]]<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gibson |first1=Owen |title=World Cup 2014: England to kick off 'group of death' in the jungle |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/dec/06/world-cup-2014-england-group-death-brazil |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=The Guardian |date=6 December 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Guillén |first1=Rafael |title=Costa Rica’s Stunning Upset in the Group of Death at Brazil 2014 |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/fifa-world-cup-2026/articles/costa-rica-s-stunning-upset-in-the-group-of-death-at-brazil-2014-2026-06-03 |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=beIN SPORTS |language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Hossain |first1=Sabbir |title=Costa Rica's spark shines in shadows of giants {{!}} The Daily Star |url=https://www.thedailystar.net/sports/sports-special/fifa-world-cup-2026/news/costa-ricas-spark-shines-shadows-giants-4180746 |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=www.thedailystar.net |date=20 May 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.theringer.com/soccer/2022/11/14/23452070/world-cup-group-of-death | title=Welcome to the World Cup Group of Death | date=14 November 2022 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Mondiali 2014: ottavi al via domani con Brasile-Cile. Ecco tutte le partite |url=https://www.gazzetta.it/Calcio/Mondiali/26-06-2014/mondiali-2014-ottavi-via-domani-brasile-cile-ecco-tutte-partite-801055236052.shtml |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=La Gazzetta dello Sport - Tutto il rosa della vita |date=2014 |language=it}}</ref> (along with Groups [[2014 FIFA World Cup Group B|B]] and [[2014 FIFA World Cup Group G|G]]),<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jackson |first1=Jamie |title=World Cup 2014 draw: Spain and Holland in 'group of death' |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/dec/06/world-cup-2014-draw-group-death-spain |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=The Guardian |date=6 December 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Daniels |first1=Tim |title=World Cup Group of Death 2014: Analyzing Most Difficult Draw in FIFA Tournament |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/1878629-world-cup-group-of-death-2014-analysing-most-difficult-draw-in-fifa-tournament |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=bleacherreport.com |date=6 December 2013 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Segura |first1=Jonathan |title=World Cup Preview: The Breakout Stars of Brazil |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/culture/culture-sports/world-cup-preview-young-gods-and-groups-of-death-71050/ |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=Rolling Stone |date=11 June 2014}}</ref> and among the "toughest" and "most memorable" groups of death in FIFA World Cup history.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ross-Murray |first1=Evan |title=The Worst Groups of Death in World Cup History |url=https://www.si.com/soccer/worst-groups-of-death-world-cup-history |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=SI |date=4 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Carrara |first1=Germán |title=Los Grupos de la Muerte más recordados en la Copa del Mundo |url=https://bolavip.com/copa-del-mundo/los-grupos-de-la-muerte-mas-recordados-en-la-copa-del-mundo |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=Bolavip |date=4 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Five of the most lethal World Cups group of death |url=https://timesofmalta.com/article/five-of-the-most-lethal-world-cups-group-of-death.664418 |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=Times of Malta |date=30 November 2017 |language=en-gb}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Duarte |first1=Maximiliano |title=Los “grupos de la muerte” que marcaron los Mundiales: los cruces históricos y las eliminaciones más dolorosas |url=https://www.c5n.com/deportes/los-grupos-la-muerte-que-marcaron-los-mundiales-los-cruces-historicos-y-las-eliminaciones-mas-dolorosas-n222887 |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=[[Canal 5 Noticias]] |date=4 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=La historia más feroz de los mundiales: los Grupos de la Muerte |url=https://www.clarosports.com/futbol/mundial-2026/la-historia-mas-feroz-de-los-mundiales-los-grupos-de-la-muerte/ |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=ClaroSports |date=6 December 2025 |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ramos |first1=Estefanía |title=Los grupos de la muerte más complicados a lo largo de la historia de los mundiales |url=https://www.90min.com/es/posts/los-grupos-de-la-muerte-mas-complicados-a-lo-largo-de-la-historia-de-los-mundiales |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=[[90min]] |date=29 March 2022 |language=es-ES}}</ref>

Play began on 14 June and ended on 24 June 2014. Costa Rica topped the group undefeated, despite being considered underdogs and expected to finish last in a group containing three former winners of the competition.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marquez |first1=Damian |title=World Cup Preview: Three former champions featured in Group D |url=https://www.visaliatimesdelta.com/story/sports/2014/06/07/world-cup-preview-three-former-champions-featured-group-d/10118961/ |access-date=9 July 2026 |work=Visalia Times-Delta |date=6 June 2014}}</ref> Of those three, Uruguay qualified second, thereby eliminating Italy and England.

