===England vs Italy===
The two teams had met in 24 previous matches, including in the [[1990 FIFA World Cup]] match for third place, won by Italy [[1990 FIFA World Cup knockout stage#Italy vs England|2–1]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf#page=14 |title=2014 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |publisher=FIFA.com |page=14 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140629232249/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/fifafacts/mencompwc/51/97/38/2014fwc_kit_matches_neutral.pdf |archive-date=29 June 2014 }}</ref> Their most recent competitive meeting was in the [[UEFA Euro 2012]] quarter-finals, won by Italy on penalties after a [[UEFA Euro 2012 knockout stage#England vs Italy|scoreless draw]].
<!--Match summary goes here, once the match is completed-->

Italy went ahead first, when from a short corner, [[Andrea Pirlo]] dummied [[Marco Verratti]]'s pass, and [[Claudio Marchisio]] scored with a low right footed shot from outside the penalty box.<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/jun/15/england-italy-world-cup-2014-group-d-match-report|title= Italy's Mario Balotelli leaves England's Group D hopes in the balance|date= 15 June 2014 |work=Guardian|access-date=30 October 2014}}</ref>
England quickly equalised through a close-range [[Daniel Sturridge]] goal from a [[Wayne Rooney]] cross from the left. The scores were level at 1–1 at half time, but [[Mario Balotelli]] headed Italy's winner from close range five minutes after play resumed from a cross by [[Antonio Candreva]] on the right.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Phil |last=McNulty |title=England 1-2 Italy |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/25285071 |publisher=BBC Sport (British Broadcasting Corporation) |date=15 June 2014 |access-date=15 June 2014 }}</ref>

The England physiotherapist [[Gary Lewin]] was stretchered off with a dislocated ankle suffered in the celebrations for England's goal, which ruled him out for the rest of the World Cup. With Italy going out in the group stages after losing against both [[Costa Rica national football team|Costa Rica]] and [[Uruguay national football team|Uruguay]] by identical 1-0 scorelines after having previously done so in [[2010 FIFA World Cup Group F|2010]] (drawing 1-1 vs both [[Paraguay national football team|Paraguay]] and [[New Zealand men's national football team|New Zealand]] after conceding the first goal of both games before trailing 2-0 and 3-1 in an eventual 3-2 defeat vs [[Slovakia national football team|Slovakia]] in that tournament), then failing to qualify for the [[2018 FIFA World Cup|next]] [[2022 FIFA World Cup|three]] [[2026 FIFA World Cup|tournaments]], this remains the latest World Cup match Italy scored a goal in, and would be the only World Cup match since winning [[2006 FIFA World Cup|2006]] they didn’t trail at any point and won in, which also makes it the only match they scored the first goal and held a lead at any point.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/27854657|title=World Cup 2014: England physio Gary Lewin out of World Cup|work=BBC Sport|date=15 June 2014}}</ref>

